What is Map (Java)?

In Java, a Map is an interface in the Java Collections Framework that stores data in key–value pairs.

Each key is unique
Each key maps to exactly one value
Values can be duplicate, but keys cannot


Types of Map in Java
1️⃣ HashMap

Does not maintain order
Allows one null key
Not synchronized
Fast performance

HashMap<Integer, String> map = new HashMap<>();



LinkedHashMap

Maintains insertion order
Allows one null key
Slightly slower than HashMap

LinkedHashMap<Integer, String> map = new LinkedHashMap<>();



TreeMap

Maintains sorted order (ascending)
Does not allow null key
Slower than HashMap (because it uses Red-Black Tree)

TreeMap<Integer, String> map = new TreeMap<>();

